{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Bind them, write them</b> — upon the Torah and the commandment, for HaShem will send His kindness and truth to the one in need, and they will not forsake you; therefore, <i>bind them</i> etc., and the reason is so that you will not forget them. Another interpretation: You act so that kindness and truth will not forsake you — <i>bind them</i> etc., and <i>find favor</i>, and you will find."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The reading ומצא פירוש appears to split into two phrases: 'and find favor' (from the verse's ומצא חן) followed by ותמצא ('and you will find'). Translated hyper-literally as the text stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:52.960755402Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}